  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm a Business Analyst at Meesho in Bengaluru, where I work across
      pricing, business finance, and marketplace analytics. I build
      discount-allocation models, P&amp;L automation, and forecasting
      pipelines in SQL and PySpark.
    </p>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      I graduated in Computer Engineering from COEP, Pune, where my thesis
      explored federated learning under data corruption, work that later
      grew into a published research paper. Before converting to a full-time
      role, I interned at Meesho on pricing elasticity and order-volume
      forecasting.
    </p>

    <h2>What I'm working on</h2>
    <p>
      Outside of work, I'm building a portfolio of end-to-end data science
      projects: from dynamic-pricing models on marketplace data to
      electricity-demand forecasting. I'm also exploring the world of embedded
      electronics, a thread that goes back to my time at the CSAT club. This site is where I write up what I learn along
      the way.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      I run a home server on repurposed hardware, was part of COEP's CubeSat
      satellite team, and occasionally race punts. You can reach me through
      the links in the box on the right.
    </p>
